+# SCOPE - RELEASE-IMPROVE-PLAN: the improvements release's design revision and plan addendum (records)
+
+Records alone, written by the supervisor in the improvements release's change cycle (~/.claude/cursor-bridge/workflow/phases/change-cycle.md) on the finished program release (2026.11.23a, installed 2026-11-24): the design revision and its plan addendum as one subject, `improvements`, through the two-critic design critique (four rounds, the ceiling, and the confirming read) and the owner's design gate (2026-11-24, four answers in the question form). No program, workflow, test or shipped bridge text changes; no builder ran. Branch design-improvements from origin/main at the merge of PR #203 (669d3b4). Thirteen files: docs/BUILD_PLAN.md, docs/DESIGN.md, docs/DESIGN_CRITIQUE.md, docs/HARDENING.md, docs/INVENTORY.md, docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md, docs/REQUIREMENTS.md, docs/diagrams/D-001 to D-004 and INDEX.md, project.json.
+
+## What the records must do
+- docs/DESIGN.md, the section "Change: the improvements release (2026-11-24)": what the release builds from the two Sunday evaluations' items (C25 to C61, T44 to T108, KP-084 to KP-100), the owner's two rules of 2026-11-15 and the diagram design-decision item; for each program item its form as built and why; the roster's alternate reviewer and the built set with its three states and its table of ten rows; the review launch's log and reply named by the snapshot; the secret-path rule; the stop hook and the question form; the rule budget; the host's facts as tables (documented, observed or to be probed, each probe with its failure form); Failure modes, Security, Testing strategy, Impact on existing behaviour with the deviations from the items' wording, Open questions as decided, Who decided.
+- docs/REQUIREMENTS.md: R-106 to R-136 added, each `planned`; R-031 and R-037 closed as the owner decided at the intake.
+- docs/BUILD_PLAN.md, "The improvements release - the plan addendum": the constraints, stages I1 to I5, 41 increments TASK-085 to TASK-118 (six of the numbers split by letters), a Demonstration and an Alters line per stage, the header's stages recomposed from the prose.
+- docs/diagrams/: D-001 to D-004 revised (labels, elements and flows for the release's programs, the built set, the launcher's two review files, the stop hook's record; D-003 gains one transition), INDEX.md.
+- docs/INVENTORY.md: the release's Decisions rows (the scope as confirmed at the intake, the word budget in the owner's words, the roster's second reviewer, the deviations, the gate's four answers).
+- docs/DESIGN_CRITIQUE.md: subject improvements, ten round entries (rounds 1 to 4 and the confirming read, two critics each), six findings accepted with their reasons, the confirming read's findings recorded as fixed, unverified, Resolution none run, the Gate line with the owner's four answers. The five round files are removed, as the procedure asks.
+- docs/HARDENING.md: the release's section (the intake, the scouts, the retirement candidates not taken, the host's facts, the leads, one entry per critique round, the survey of the existing tests, the gate).
+- docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md as it will read at this pull request's merge (ISS-009; cap 12,000 characters): Phase changing, the change cycle's step the loop from TASK-085, In flight none, Awaiting user on nothing, Remote sync naming this pull request's merge, Last reflection this gate's. project.json: the state's stage.
+
+## Tests
+None is added or changed, and there is no mutants file and no mutation driver. The tests that read these records are the repository's own: tests/test_release_b_bootstrap.py reads the status file as a pull request into main; tests/test_d003_review_round_states.py, tests/test_diagram_check.py, tests/test_header_tables.py, tests/test_header_plan.py, tests/test_header_status.py, tests/test_release_t_records.py and tests/test_text_consistency.py read the diagrams and the records' headers; tests/test_running_projects_classify.py and tests/test_type_host_extension.py hold the status file's `Workflows:` line, which this diff does not change.
+
+## What to check
+- Each claim is true against the repository: run `~/.claude/cursor-bridge/plan-check.py` (RESULT: OK, 125 increments, 84 merged, notes on 28 large increments, READY naming TASK-085 first), `~/.claude/cursor-bridge/completion-check.py --mode plan` (RESULT: OK; 105 built, 31 planned), `~/.claude/cursor-bridge/inventory-check.py` (RESULT: OK; status 28 lines), `~/.claude/cursor-bridge/diagram-check.py --mode design` and `--mode code` (RESULT: OK, 5 selected, 13 omitted) and `~/.claude/cursor-bridge/workflow-check.py --status docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md` (RESULT: OK). `completion-check.py --mode done` names the planned rows: that is not this pull request's defect.
+- The records agree with each other and with the programs they name under bridge/cursor-bridge/ as those stand today: every row R-106 to R-136 is planned and stands on some increment's Satisfies line; what the design says a program does today (roster-check.py's `built_by` reading the last builder run of the branch, bridge-run.py's `review_family_refusal` noting a failure and launching, the run record's row holding a key `head` that is the command's program name, `built_by` skipping a line that does not parse, bridge-install.py's `merge_settings` adding a hook group only where it holds a command the file lacks, session-start.py's `MAX_OUTPUT` and `cap`, loop-guard.py allowing every continued stop) is what the file holds; the design, R-107, D-003, D-004 and TASK-086a and TASK-086b state the built set alike (which run is dropped, the unknown set, the set that cannot be read and its four causes inside a repository, a folder in no repository); the design, R-129, D-004 and TASK-110a state the stop hook's chain alike; the status file's position lines read as at this merge, its header equals its body, and its Phase equals project.json's.
+- Nothing in the records weakens a gate that stands: no sentence lets a reviewer of a family that built a change review it, lets a merge happen without the proof that CI passed on the merged head, or widens what a builder may write.
+- No computer path, user name or e-mail address in a tracked file (rule 54). The Documents/ folder is outside git and no part of this diff.
+
+## The threat model
+docs/INVENTORY.md's Decisions record none for what this diff changes, which is records. For the parts the plan's increments will change, the inventory records the review guard's threat model (KP-032, R-050: what a reviewer does in passing in the checkout is inside it, a deliberate reach past it is recorded and never blocking by itself), the session-start hook's (a partial, mismatched or hand-edited install, not a hostile checker or module) and, for GitHub's replies, outside input to the rule's reader; the design's Security section says what the new readers trust and names the limits that stay (the run record lies in the checkout, where a builder or a reviewer can write). The five blocking classes stand.
+
+## Before this round
+- The design critique: plan-critic and Review B (grok-4.7-medium, design mode) read the subject in rounds 1 to 4 and in the confirming read. Every finding was fixed except six accepted with a recorded reason. The confirming read held one Blocking finding of each critic (plan-critic 1 / 2 / 4, Review B 1 / 3 / 0), each fixed; those fixes are recorded as fixed, unverified, since no critic has read them. The owner approved the whole at the design gate. Review B checks the merge gate's points here, not the design's or the plan's choices again.
+- The records and diagram tests on this head's records: twenty-one files in a stripped run (the nineteen that read the headers, the diagrams and the records, with tests/test_running_projects_classify.py and tests/test_type_host_extension.py), and tests/test_release_b_bootstrap.py alone with a pull request's variables set, their counts in the pull request's description. The whole suite was not run locally: it is CI's, on this pull request.
+- Review A (diff-reviewer, claude-opus-5-5) read the change at 131759f: APPROVE, no Blocking finding, two Should fix and six Consider, each taken in the one records commit after it (docs/HARDENING.md, the bullet "The records pull request's gate", lists them): TASK-086a's four limits; the words "where the tree holds a report file" before the base that cannot be found, in three sentences; today's behaviour of the launcher on a line that does not parse, stated as the code has it; the run record's `head` key as the command's program name; the addendum's opening; stage I5's demonstration with R-115 deferred; the evaluated stop in R-129 and D-004; the status file's sentence on the model switch. By its own account it did not read docs/DESIGN.md's parts on the mutation engine, the review guard, the permission guard and the checkers, the bodies of TASK-088 to TASK-109 and TASK-111a to TASK-113, or the diffs of D-001 and D-002. No reviewer has read that commit's eight fixes: this round is their first reading.
+
+The improvements release's increments (TASK-085 to TASK-118) are later work, not this pull request's defect. This is Review B's round 1, below the ceiling.
